AUTHORIZE keyword

Manages the users. Needs SECURITY.

  AUTHORIZE LIST [user]     lists the users, their homes, privileges, flags
  AUTHORIZE ADD user        adds a user and asks for the password twice
  AUTHORIZE MODIFY user     changes a user
  AUTHORIZE REMOVE user     removes a user. You cannot remove yourself.
                            The home folder stays on the card.

Qualifiers of ADD and MODIFY:
  /PASSWORD          asks for a new password twice, hidden as you type
  /PRIVS=(p,...)     SYSTEM, OPER, SECURITY, READALL; /NOPRIVS for none
  /HOME=folder       the home folder under SD0:[HOME]
  /DISABLED          the user cannot log in; /NODISABLED undoes it
  /NOHACKABLE        the user is never a target of the password game

A password is never typed on the command line. Changes apply at the
user's next login.

At least one enabled user keeps SYSTEM or SECURITY. A change that
would leave none is refused and nothing is written.

No folder is ever deleted or moved. ADD uses a home folder that is
there already. A new /HOME leaves the old folder: copy its files by
hand.
